I am back in the flat.
It is afternoon in Berlin.
In Mexico, it is morning now.
My table is small.
I sit at the table and open the laptop.
My laptop is ready.
I lay the chocolate on the table.
It lies next to the laptop now.
That is a surprise.
I test the camera.
The picture is good.
My room is bright.
A window is in the background.
I start the video call.
It rings.
Who is already awake?
Is my mother there?
Is my father also there?
I wait.
